artifacts are licensed at the benchmark-family level.

Component licensing
-------------------

- Source code in this repository: MIT License.
- benchmarks/VRPTW/Sintef2008: MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided
  under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The underlying
  classical VRPTW benchmark definitions originate from Solomon (1987),
  Gehring and Homberger (1999), and the SINTEF VRPTW benchmark convention.
- benchmarks/VRPTW/Dimacs2021: MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided
  under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The benchmark
  contract follows the 12th DIMACS Implementation Challenge VRPTW rules.
- benchmarks/VRPTW/Ortec2022: ORTEC instances and related redistributed BKS
  files are provided under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
  International (CC BY-NC 4.0).
- benchmarks/TDVRPTW/Dabia2013 and benchmarks/TDVRP/Dabia2013: MAMUT-routing
  curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the
  relevant rights. The underlying Solomon-derived IGP instances are those
  distributed with the MIT-licensed open-source solver of Lera-Romero,
  Miranda Bront and Soulignac (2020).
- benchmarks/TDVRPTW/Ari2018 and benchmarks/TDVRP/Ari2018: MAMUT-routing
  curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the
  relevant rights. The underlying benchmark definitions originate from the
  time-dependent TSPTW generator of the Arigliano et al. lineage.
- benchmarks/TDVRPTW/Vu2020 and benchmarks/TDVRP/Vu2020: MAMUT-routing
  curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the
  relevant rights. The underlying raw files originate from the Vu et al.
  (2020) time-dependent TSPTW benchmark material.
- benchmarks/TDVRPTW/Rifki2020 and benchmarks/TDVRP/Rifki2020: MAMUT-routing
  curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the
  relevant rights. The underlying stepwise travel-time construction follows
  Rifki et al. (2020); coordinates are a deterministic MAMUT-routing
  embedding.
- benchmarks/TDVRPTW/Lera2026 and benchmarks/TDVRP/Lera2026: MAMUT-routing
  generation and curation artifacts are provided under MIT where
  MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The base data are the Gehring and
  Homberger (1999) instances as curated in benchmarks/VRPTW/Sintef2008, with
  IGP (Ichoua-Gendreau-Potvin 2003) travel speeds.
- benchmarks/Poryos2026 (CVRP, VRPTW, TDVRP and TDVRPTW layers): OSM-derived
  benchmark instances, sidecars, generated route artifacts, and related
  benchmark data are distributed under ODbL 1.0 where they derive from
  OpenStreetMap data.
- benchmarks/Mamut2026 (CVRP): OSM-derived benchmark instances, sidecars,
  generated route artifacts, and related benchmark data are distributed under
  ODbL 1.0 where they derive from OpenStreetMap data.

Attribution
-----------

OpenStreetMap-derived artifacts use data from OpenStreetMap and its
contributors. OpenStreetMap data is available under the Open Data Commons Open
Database License: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

ORTEC benchmark artifacts are derived from the EURO Meets NeurIPS 2022 Vehicle
Routing Competition material and retain the original CC BY-NC 4.0 terms:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

The website workbench map uses the CARTO Positron and Dark Matter basemaps,
